[size=5][b]psi_autocast_mfd: an in-game psi macro MFD[/b][/size]

Remaster only.
Plan your psionics and build [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/systemshock225thanniversaryremaster/mods/20]psi-autocast[/url] macros without leaving the game, in an MFD HUD in the game's own cyberpunk style.
SCP compatible.

[b]A restart is the most you'll ever have to do: no manual edits, if you don't want them.[/b]

[line]
[size=4][b]What it shows[/b][/size]
A scrolling table of all 35 disciplines, each with its icon, tier and name, and:
[list]
[*][b]Duration[/b] at your current PSI and at PSI 8.[/*]
[*][b]Effect[/b] at your current PSI and at PSI 8: damage, healing, stat bonus, chance or recharge, whichever the discipline has.[/*]
[*][b]Overload[/b]: what an overload gives you, for the disciplines that benefit from one.[/*]
[*][b]Cyber Mods[/b]: "bought", or what it costs, including every tier you still need to unlock to reach it (adjusted per difficulty).[/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Building macros[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Pick a key, or click [b]Keys[/b] to choose one from a keyboard that shows what every key does.[/*]
[*]Click disciplines to add casts, add psi hypos, waits and a finishing weapon switch.[/*]
[*][b]Save[/b], close the MFD, and press the key. The psi_autocast mod runs the macro.[/*]
[/list]
Every key that isn't set by the game is a macro key, ready on the next keypress after you save. Keys you free later in the game's Controls menu become macro keys from your next start. Keys the game uses stay with the Controls menu.

[line]
[size=4][b]Extras[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Worm skin swap[/b] (off until you tick it): while any macro runs, you wear the worm skin, if you have one, and your own armor goes back on afterwards. After Molecular Duplication, Electron Cascade or Molecular Transmutation, it waits while the cursor is up, so the worm skin is still on when you click the item.[/*]
[*][b]K uses a maintenance tool[/b] on the weapon in your hand: no dragging.[/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Setup[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install and enable [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/systemshock225thanniversaryremaster/mods/20]psi_autocast[/url] 1.4 or later.[/*]
[*]Extract this mod into the [b]game folder[/b], the one with [b]SystemShock2Remastered.exe[/b] (not the save folder). It adds [i]mods\psi_autocast_mfd.kpf[/i].[/*]
[*]New Game → Mods → add [b]psi_autocast_mfd[/b] (keep psi_autocast) → Apply → start, then load your save and make a regular save.[/*]
[*]On that first load the MFD sets up your keys: keypad * to open it, keypad + to cancel a running macro, K for the maintenance tool, and every free key as a macro key. Restart the game once when it tells you to, then press keypad * to open the MFD HUD.[/*]
[*][b]In a new game, wait until you're through training before using the MFD:[/b] macros don't take before then.[/*]
[/list]
If you'd rather set keys up yourself, you still can:

Setup Script (GitHub only):
[spoiler][size=4][b]The setup script[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/feygon/SS2PsiAutocastMFD/releases/latest]setupPsiMfd.bat[/url], from the GitHub release, sets up many keys at once. Run it with the game closed. It:
[list]
[*]binds keypad * to open the MFD, and keypad + to psi_autocast's cancel and K to the maintenance tool if they're free;[/*]
[*]gives G and J psi_autocast's two starter casts, as macros you can edit;[/*]
[*]makes every free key a macro key;[/*]
[*]asks (y/n) about bound keys whose job is also on another key, and about letting the mouse wheel scroll the MFD;[/*]
[*]never uses reserved keys;[/*]
[*]backs up [i]user.bnd[/i] first, and adds only what's missing if you run it again.[/*]
[/list]
[/spoiler]
Manual Setup:
[spoiler][size=4][b]The user.bnd lines[/b][/size]
[i]user.bnd[/i] is in [i]%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Nightdive Studios\System Shock 2 Remastered\[/i]. Back it up, then edit it with the game closed.

One key opens and closes the MFD, and one uses a maintenance tool:
[code]bind keypad_star "summon_obj PsiMfd"
bind k "summon_obj PsiMfdMaintainWeapon"[/code]
Each macro key runs its own file. Add one line per key you want, changing the key and the file name together:
[code]bind keypad_minus "run user:/psi_macros\Macro_keypad_minus.cmd"
bind keypad_del "run user:/psi_macros\Macro_keypad_del.cmd"[/code]

Optional: the mouse wheel scrolls the MFD when the cursor is over it, and switches weapons everywhere else. Replace the two [i]mouse_wheel[/i] lines with:
[code]bind mouse_wheel_up "summon_obj PsiMfdWheelUp"
bind mouse_wheel_down "summon_obj PsiMfdWheelDown"[/code]
In a save without psi_autocast_mfd enabled, the wheel then doesn't switch weapons. To undo, put back [i]bind mouse_wheel_up "cycle_weapon 1"[/i] and [i]bind mouse_wheel_down "cycle_weapon -1"[/i].[/spoiler]
[line]
[size=4][b]What it writes[/b][/size]
Macros go in [i]Saved Games\Nightdive Studios\System Shock 2 Remastered\psi_macros\[/i], one small text file per key, and the worm skin swap choice in [i]psi_mfd_settings.txt[/i] there. Key bindings go in [i]user.bnd[/i], backed up first as [i]user.bnd.mfd_backup[/i].

The mod itself is seven text files: no images, nothing downloaded. The discipline icons and the MFD's background are the remaster's own art, loaded from the game at runtime.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]System Shock 2: 25th Anniversary Remaster on PC. Tested on the Epic version, game version 1.3.4984.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/systemshock225thanniversaryremaster/mods/20]psi_autocast[/url] mod v1.4 or later.[/*]
[/list]
Tested alongside the remaster's bundled mods (SCP beta 6, SHTUP, Four Hundred, patch_ext). Multiplayer is untested.

